  "commands": [
    "CRYPTO-LOCK-IDENTITY: reviewed the exact immutable commit in a separate detached checkout; tracked and untracked status clean before review and after removing review-only dependency links.",
    "CRYPTO-LOCK-INVENTORY: independently recomputed 234 preserved source hashes and 702 historical Git blob comparisons across the original reviewed, DCO publication and integrated trees; verified their tree equality and the owner protocol projection.",
    "CRYPTO-LOCK-TRANSITION: compared every catalog field; exactly fifteen candidate-to-locked transitions remove only their satisfied review records, 105 other rows remain equal, counts are 114 locked and six candidate.",
    "CRYPTO-LOCK-PROVENANCE: recomputed all four public role record digests and their historical repository hashes, including 536 cryptography inputs; matched the immutable original cryptography verdict and 18 archived execution artifacts. Prior independent preimage/signature oracles are explicitly reused, not rerun.",
    "CRYPTO-LOCK-PIN: independently recomputed the serialized evidence pin and rejected individual byte corruption in all 240 protected inputs.",
    "CRYPTO-LOCK-SNAPSHOT: independently reproduced six alternating-map bypasses and a backing-buffer parsing failure; the ordinary-map negative control rejects each extra promotion.",
    "CRYPTO-LOCK-GATE: reproduced the repository specification-lock gate under the qualified Bun revision; 25 tests passed, 139 assertions, zero failures and 100 percent reported function/line coverage for the four included modules.",
    "CRYPTO-LOCK-ENVELOPE: validate this record with the byte-identical original validator and exact job; reject four mismatched identity controls."
  ],
  "findings": {
    "blocking": [
      {
        "title": "SEC-LOCK-01: verified baseline bytes are not the parsed baseline bytes",
        "detail": "tools/quality/specification-lock.ts:54-60 hashes a caller-owned ReadonlyMap entry, then reads it again to parse the baseline. Independent probes return authentic bytes on the first read and a fabricated catalog on the second: each of the six unrelated candidate authorities can become a sixteenth promotion without failure. Mutation of the original buffer after hashing also affects parsing. SHA-256 is not broken; the verified-input/use binding is. This independently reproduced, already reported security defect blocks specification promotion. It does not establish an execution capability or a weakness in unchanged signature/preimage specifications."
      }
    ],
    "major": [],
    "minor": [],
    "nonBlocking": []
  },
  "residualRisks": [
    "This is only the cryptography specialized promotion review. Other required roles, final integration checks and the actual owner control milestone remain separate. No runtime activation, real signer, authority adapter, consumer conformance or data-processing admission is granted.",
    "The owner-control JSON and embedded role files are pinned audit inputs, not signatures authenticating a human decision. Git identifiers and SHA-256 pins establish content identity under the reviewed trust anchor; they do not establish production permission or historic organizational membership.",
    "The canonical bodies, signature domains, detached records, handoff/binding/plan/mission/authorization preimages, strict-Ed25519 vectors, schemas and SDK projections remain byte-identical. Heavy prior crypto oracles and root checks were not rerun in this pass; their immutable results are reused only for those unchanged inputs. The new gate received fresh targeted tests and independent adversarial probes.",
    "Private review dependencies reused an existing frozen installation with an identical committed lock. No new dependency install, browser, network execution or product source change occurred. This is not a clean-room dependency supply-chain attestation.",
    "This verdict remains reject. A successor may reuse unchanged cryptographic authority and historical oracle evidence only after fresh commit/hash equality checks. Its input snapshot correction, adversarial regressions, exact job identity and final promotion gates require a new review record; this record cannot be retargeted."
  ],
  "verdict": "reject",
